@startuml Feature Flags Sequence Diagram

title Feature Flags Workflow

actor User
participant "Application" as App
participant "Feature Flag Service" as FFS
participant "Developer" as Dev
participant "Monitoring System" as Mon

note right: Feature flags allow dynamic control of application behavior without code changes

User -> App: Request feature
App -> FFS: Check feature flag status
FFS --> App: Return flag value (true/false)

alt Flag is enabled
    App -> App: Execute new feature logic
    App --> User: Show new feature UI
    note right: New feature is active for this user
else Flag is disabled
    App -> App: Execute old feature logic
    App --> User: Show old feature UI
    note right: Fallback to existing behavior
end

App -> Mon: Log feature usage metrics

note over Dev: Developer monitors feature performance

Dev -> FFS: Update flag configuration
note right: Adjust targeting rules, percentage rollout, etc.

Dev -> Mon: Review analytics
Mon --> Dev: Provide insights (conversion rates, errors)

alt Feature successful
    Dev -> FFS: Gradually increase rollout
    note right: Increase percentage from 10% to 100%
else Issues detected
    Dev -> FFS: Disable flag immediately
    note right: Emergency rollback without redeployment
end

note over Dev, FFS: Once feature is stable, flag can be removed from code

@enduml